{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united","id":1150564,"title":"What can the dragonblooded host do when united?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-18T00:42:15-07:00","id":1150564,"title":"What can the dragonblooded host do when united?","content":"So! The realm. <br /> <br /> Let's say that the scarlet empress, for some reason, decides to change her tactics. She removes some officials, and removes others. She institutes a culture of cooperation and collaboration, backed by propaganda and dynasty charms. And her first order is: take over Creation. <br /> <br /> So... how much improved is this Realm? Can they do it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T05:50:22-07:00","id":1150616,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a great way to overextend the Realm in a way that implodes it and lets the Lunars waltz right in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-18-2017, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T06:39:24-07:00","id":1150623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150616#post1150616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a great way to overextend the Realm in a way that implodes it and lets the Lunars waltz right in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. <br /> <br /> Perhaps the op needed more thought...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T08:31:10-07:00","id":1150648,"title":"","content":"A truly coordinated, harmonious Realm would be a nightmare for everyone facing it. Younger Sidereals, who had only seen the vague shadows of what the Anathema are capable of in the Wyld Hunt would now perceive echoes of the terrible force brought to bear for the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> Alucard is absolutely right that the ambition of taking over Creation is one that could weaken the Realm and expose weaknesses. But a considerable amount of House resources are expended on the cloak-and-dagger games they play amongst themselves and the bribes and counter-bribes that are a part of life from their birth. Likewise, the Thousand Mazy Paths are deliberately byzantine and inefficient; some sort of bureaucratic reckoning would probably result in a stronger infrastructure that would, in the long run, make for a stronger Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T09:16:06-07:00","id":1150665,"title":"","content":"World conquest is an achievable goal, but it would probably take centuries and during that time a supermajority of the Dragonblooded population would need to be committed to the plan. That's a tall order by itself, but the inevitable intervention of other supernatural beings makes everything much more complicated. The Lunars are only the start - you can expect resistance from all manner of gods and their cults, from empowered rulers like the Perfect of Paragon, and from the Exalted champions of other nations.<br /> <br /> That's not to say it couldn't be done, but I very much doubt it would be as simple as &quot;Step 1. The DBs get their shit together. Step 2. ROTFLSTOMP everything.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T09:58:48-07:00","id":1150675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united#post1150564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So! The realm. <br /> <br /> Let's say that the scarlet empress, for some reason, decides to change her tactics. She removes some officials, and removes others. She institutes a culture of cooperation and collaboration, backed by propaganda and dynasty charms. And her first order is: take over Creation. <br /> <br /> So... how much improved is this Realm? Can they do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'm not sure you could do that. The Realm is set up as it is largely because the Scarlet Empress cannot control it if it were more efficient, so she makes sure that the various power blocs waste their energy on each other rather than building up power so one can take over. <br /> <br /> That said, if she could unite everyone under the banner of taking over the world, make everything more efficient, and so on, I could imagine that they could significantly increase their current borders temporarily, but holding on to all that territory is a completely different story. The amount of pushback and guerrilla warfair they'd have to deal with would increase substantially because everyone else would get serious too.<br /> <br /> I mean, technically, the Realm has won every war they've ever had in the Scavenger Lands, but, because they've never been able to invade Lookshy city and both Nexus and Great Forks have powerful spirit protectors who refuse to bend to the Empress, they haven't been able to hold the territory. I feel like there would be a lot of that going on in your hypothetical case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T10:02:10-07:00","id":1150676,"title":"","content":"This video might be worth watching, if you want a better idea as to why the Realm is set up like it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rStL7niR7gs\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rStL7niR7gs\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rStL7niR7gs\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/rStL7niR7gs </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T10:29:31-07:00","id":1150691,"title":"","content":"The Realm more or less <i>is</i> what the Dragon-Blooded host can do when united. (They'd be better off if they didn't have to constantly fight the Lunars, of course.)<br /> <br /> And, as the video BrilliantRain linked implies, the things you're suggesting the Empress do away with are the mechanisms she uses to keep them unified - do away with them and you have the Realm falling into petty squabbling or even civil war. Cooperation and collaboration in the way you're thinking of means giving more Dragon-Blooded more power. These Dragon-Blooded will eventually have their own ideas and want to go in their own directions, which will make it harder for the Empress to retain centralized control and make the entire thing less unified.<br /> <br /> Basically your stated goal and the things you're suggesting are at odds. Complete unity and freedom are at odds with each other; by definition, a unified DB host is one where most DBs have little individual power or say in the direction of the state as as a whole. If that seems awful, keep in mind that your first suggestion for what they'd do with that unity is stomp everyone else into submission with a giant elemental-flavored boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T10:48:13-07:00","id":1150697,"title":"","content":"... a conga line that was MILES long, I bet!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:07:36-07:00","id":1150704,"title":"","content":"Ah Dynasty charms.<br /> With the level of brainwashing the Empress was capable of in RotSE she could easily get tweak the Immaculate texts to give Solars and Lunars a place in the Scarlet Empire similar to what Exigents now benefit from.<br /> <br /> Without that almost hive mind level of unity the bigger question is what circumstances united them in the first place.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">*Disclaimer: I don't like Dynasty charms or RotSE's portrayal of them in her hands, I feel they turned one of the greatest political minds in the setting into an ant queen who rules through her vagina (seriously she's been noted as being able to use them to convince Dynasts to undergo the investiture of Infernal Glory!). They also take an unfortunate trend with gender in the 2e Realm's leadership and make it even worse, where the female Great House leaders - Mnemon, V'neef and the Cynis sisters are ruling over their direct decedents while the male Great House leaders (Cathak Cainan and Ragara Banoba) achieved their positions of power through personal merit. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:18:54-07:00","id":1150709,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not sure if the Realm could really do that. The Empress spent 7 centuries creating this system. Every Dragon Blooded, even (or perhaps especially) her own children have internalized the understanding that their success comes as someone else's loss,and that someone else's loss can become their own success. Many of the powerful Dragon Blooded have gotten to where they are through some level of success in the Realm's inner-conflict. I think if the Empress waved her hands and said, &quot;No more fighting,&quot; it wouldn't amount to much. It would take decades or centuries to change the philosophies and ideas that so many Dragon Blooded have.<br /> <br /> While there is a lot of talk about the ideals of the &quot;Upright Soldier&quot; in reality few Realm Dragon Blooded really follow those rules. If the Empress began changing the culture to where those ideals (service, loyalty, brotherhood, etc) were the attributes that led to better positions and praise, you might see the Realm become more militaristic and powerful. A truly united, focused and directed Realm would be able to extend its power, perhaps even finally conquer the Scavenger Lands. Fortunately for the rest of Creation, that just isn't terribly plausible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T11:38:28-07:00","id":1150717,"title":"","content":"What can they do? The chief result of Dragonblooded unification will always be Dragonblooded cold civil war, and plotting to take over the unified host (and it's all very interesting)! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Perhaps less jokingly, this reminds me of an old debate here (or on the old WW forum), which I should perhaps not mention, about what it was even possible that the Dragonblooded could achieve, if unified, working together, fully embracing their potential in the right way:<br /> <br /> In the Red Corner: &quot;The Dragonblooded should not be able to achieve a much more sophisticated, better off, well developed society than the Realm, roughly, is, or The Shogunate roughly was (and the Shogunate was on a clear trajectory to become something not much more than the Realm). <br /> <br /> The core idea of Exalted is that only the return of the glorious Solar Kings can bring a meaningful Golden Age back to humanity. That sets limits on what the Dragonblooded should be allowed to achieve. <br /> <br /> (What's the point of being a glorious Solar god-king returned to the world to bring a Golden Age if your lesser usurper totally have the potential to build a lesser Golden Age without you?)&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the Blue Corner: &quot;If we extrapolate from the potential of Terrestrial Circle Sorcery, Terrestrial Circle Artificing, Dragonblooded social genius, and look at the myriad sources of wild magic and sheer possibility in the world of Exalted, we can imagine that a Dragonblooded society for which everything goes right, culturally, can achieve human welfare and sophistication well beyond the Age of Sorrows, and perhaps even beyond the present day Real World. <br /> <br /> Thematic unity be damned, conservation of internal consistency to the established badassdom of the Dragonblooded, and openness to a world full of potential, clearly allows for the possibility.&quot;. <br /> <br /> This was never really resolved (though, truthfully as a person who preferred the Blue option, I have to say that Red tended to get many more forum likes). This was back in the days of Second, mind, so this thinking may simply be completely out of date today.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T15:34:43-07:00","id":1150812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150717#post1150717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Perhaps less jokingly, this reminds me of an old debate here (or on the old WW forum), which I should perhaps not mention, about what it was even possible that the Dragonblooded could achieve, if unified, working together, fully embracing their potential in the right way:</div> </div> </div> </div>Much like the Vision of Gold, it could have played out like that (especially with the Blue Corner), but then it wouldn't be this game anymore, so it didn't.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T15:37:55-07:00","id":1150814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150717#post1150717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can they do? The chief result of Dragonblooded unification will always be Dragonblooded cold civil war, and plotting to take over the unified host (and it's all very interesting)! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Perhaps less jokingly, this reminds me of an old debate here (or on the old WW forum), which I should perhaps not mention, about what it was even possible that the Dragonblooded could achieve, if unified, working together, fully embracing their potential in the right way:<br /> <br /> In the Red Corner: &amp;quot;The Dragonblooded should not be able to achieve a much more sophisticated, better off, well developed society than the Realm, roughly, is, or The Shogunate roughly was (and the Shogunate was on a clear trajectory to become something not much more than the Realm).<br /> <br /> The core idea of Exalted is that only the return of the glorious Solar Kings can bring a meaningful Golden Age back to humanity. That sets limits on what the Dragonblooded should be allowed to achieve.<br /> <br /> (What's the point of being a glorious Solar god-king returned to the world to bring a Golden Age if your lesser usurper totally have the potential to build a lesser Golden Age without you?)&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> In the Blue Corner: &amp;quot;If we extrapolate from the potential of Terrestrial Circle Sorcery, Terrestrial Circle Artificing, Dragonblooded social genius, and look at the myriad sources of wild magic and sheer possibility in the world of Exalted, we can imagine that a Dragonblooded society for which everything goes right, culturally, can achieve human welfare and sophistication well beyond the Age of Sorrows, and perhaps even beyond the present day Real World.<br /> <br /> Thematic unity be damned, conservation of internal consistency to the established badassdom of the Dragonblooded, and openness to a world full of potential, clearly allows for the possibility.&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> This was never really resolved (though, truthfully as a person who preferred the Blue option, I have to say that Red tended to get many more forum likes). This was back in the days of Second, mind, so this thinking may simply be completely out of date today.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Why could it infact not be both? Based upon what kind of story the players and ST wish to shape? I could see for instance the red corner making for an epic chronicle of a circle of solar exalted bringing a new golden age just as easily as I could see the blue corner being an amazing chronicle for a circle of Dragonblooded who wanted to carve a new path for humanity away from the past. Both can concepts can exist in the world, as Exalted is not a simulation but a narrative tale between the ST and players. *shrug*. I guess I prefer a scenario where both are possible based upon what the ST and players want, since it\u2019s nkt like it intrudes on another saga.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","user":"Saipjas","date":". 10-18-2017, 08:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:07:29-07:00","id":1150830,"title":"","content":"So the realm is the best the dragonblooded can make?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T17:29:54-07:00","id":1150839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150830#post1150830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So the realm is the best the dragonblooded can make?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm is <i>probably</i> the best the Dragon-Blooded can make, <i>under present circumstances, and for some definitions of &quot;best.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T18:17:29-07:00","id":1150852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150839#post1150839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm is <i>probably</i> the best the Dragon-Blooded can make, <i>under present circumstances, and for some definitions of &amp;quot;best.&amp;quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Well..... that's kinda unfortunate. My main idea was that the dragonblooded were hobbled by the empress's need for job security. If they truly worked together, if they truly stood as one, they couls bring in a new age. So what if a single dragonblooded can not take down a solar dawn or match a twilight in artifact making. If one is not enough, there are ten thousand dragons to do so. <br /> <br /> But if what is here is true, then the terrestrials are fractuous. Needing a celestial to lead them to do anything great. And that is rather..... deprotagonizing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T18:29:42-07:00","id":1150859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150852#post1150852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My main idea was that the dragonblooded were hobbled by the empress's need for job security.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's part of it, yes. Other parts of it include the nature of the Realm being an empire, the logistics of being separated from the world you intend to conquer by thousands of miles of open ocean, the presence of potent hostile powers, and <i>human nature</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150852#post1150852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they truly worked together, if they truly stood as one, they couls bring in a new age.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's awful hard for ten thousand to &quot;stand as one&quot; <i>while one is standing on nine thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine</i>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150852#post1150852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what if a single dragonblooded can not take down a solar dawn or match a twilight in artifact making. If one is not enough, there are ten thousand dragons to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, and just maybe think about this here, maybe don't obsess over comparing their respective capabilities?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150852#post1150852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But if what is here is true, then the terrestrials are fractuous.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>People</i> are a fractious bunch, and the Dragon-Blooded are people.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150852#post1150852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Needing a celestial to lead them to do anything great.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Realm <i>is</i> great, and terrible as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150852#post1150852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that is rather..... deprotagonizing</div> </div> </div> </div>If that were true, maybe, but as it stands\u2026 not really, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-18-2017, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T18:37:57-07:00","id":1150861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150852#post1150852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well..... that's kinda unfortunate. My main idea was that the dragonblooded were hobbled by the empress's need for job security. If they truly worked together, if they truly stood as one, they couls bring in a new age. So what if a single dragonblooded can not take down a solar dawn or match a twilight in artifact making. If one is not enough, there are ten thousand dragons to do so. <br /> <br /> But if what is here is true, then the terrestrials are fractuous. Needing a celestial to lead them to do anything great. And that is rather..... deprotagonizing</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you misunderstand.... the Terrestrials aren't able to do much better because they are exalted not inspite of it. Getting independent people to work together is already herding cats, Exalts are by nature super-cats that can change the world to their whim and do not like other cats. An exalt is a hero and protagonist, no one wants to play second fiddle to another guy just because they happen to be the same kind of exalt. Hell even siblings compete for the spotlight.<br /> <br /> The Solars can barely keep a circle together. Lunars do not typically lead kingdoms in groups and the sids are permanently trying to poison each other's drinks. That the dragon-blooded can keep that many Exalts in anything resembling a coherent state is already a testament to being the 'best' at teamwork.<br /> <br /> Also... the first age was a team effort by the entire host, not just the celestials. Hence it was both incredibly awesome and incredibly sucky. The kindest interpretation is basically a useless UN building supernukes to kill time while several hundred states did whatever suited them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 10-18-2017, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T18:43:49-07:00","id":1150863,"title":"","content":"To add on to what the others are saying, there is nothing stopping a storyteller for writing the chronicle of a circle of dragon-blooded from creating a new path. As TheCountAlucard said, its about where game start occurs that its probable its the best they can achieve. But I would recall the design philosophy the Devs had, specifically the call out on page 179. This limitation does NOT apply to what the protagonists of the chronicle can accomplish. Specifically <br /> <span style=\"font-family:DIN Alternate\"><span style=\"font-size:9px\">&quot;To be clear, players\u2019 characters are likely to be exceptional individuals relative to other Chosen.&quot;</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-18T22:13:25-07:00","id":1150897,"title":"","content":"While I get what people are saying about the setting here, and I say them too, I feel it's not really in the spirit of the question as it is originally asked.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the purposes of the person's thought experiment, I would say it's all right to assume that any necessary factors, even if they're somewhat unlikely (while not being implausible or impossible) are in place, and moving on from there.<br /> <br /> So:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united#post1150564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So... how much improved is this Realm? Can they do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think the resulting Realm still lives in about the same way, but possibly slightly more oppressed; I imagine that many peasants and commoners are able to leverage some advantages out of the disputes between the Exalted, and having them all be a lot more cooperative makes that task more difficult. Like how monopolies or a small number of corporations that engage in secret agreements for standard practices ultimately hurts consumers; without competition, typical people don't have much option to &quot;shop around&quot;, as it were.<br /> <br /> \u200bFor the second question, I would say that they can't, but that owes more to the world than it does to the Dragon Blooded. Cooperation might mean that somewhat more Exalted live long enough to propagate, but Dragon Blooded numbers still grow slowly, and the world is still big and complex, and home to many powers that can operate outside of their range of effective operation.<br /> <br /> \u200bNot just the Lunar Exalted, either; take the Dreaming Sea as an example of a zone that virtually no form of the Realm (unless it has a significantly altered level of First Age Artifice, and even that might be a stretch) can effectively control to a degree that I would assume necessary to qualify as &quot;taking over the world&quot;, owing to its native powers and the geographic obstacles it presents.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T03:35:21-07:00","id":1150944,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is less that the terrestrials can't conquer the whole world without the celestials leading them and more that they can't conquer the whole world with the celestials <i>standing in the way</i>.<br /> <br /> If they could co-operate, maybe form a more egalitarian relationship than the first age with solars and lunars as Alchemical-style &quot;champions&quot; that ultimately answer to the people, then yeah, they could totally do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T04:42:33-07:00","id":1150951,"title":"","content":"No number of helpful Exalted will make the world any smaller. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> .....<br /> <br /> \u200bBarring occasions where part of the plan literally entails making the world small enough for a single polity to effectively govern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T08:51:21-07:00","id":1151028,"title":"","content":"They might conquer it, but not hold it, anyway. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T10:20:03-07:00","id":1151055,"title":"","content":"How on board with this plan do you imagine the DB to be? Are they going to put an end to their extravagant lifestyles and invest similar productive resource in First Age artifice like Lookshy does? Are they going to spend some social charms getting the mortal population of the Blessed Isle on board and trust them with some of the nicer pieces of kit like Gunzosha armor? The society of the Realm is complex and a lot of pieces act as roadblocks to expansion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T23:54:14-07:00","id":1151230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150676#post1150676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This video might be worth watching, if you want a better idea as to why the Realm is set up like it is.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/rStL7niR7gs\" target=\"_blank\">https://youtu.be/rStL7niR7gs</a></div> </div> </div> </div>I really need to read The Dictator's Handbook...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T02:14:04-07:00","id":1151246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150852#post1150852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well..... that's kinda unfortunate. My main idea was that the dragonblooded were hobbled by the empress's need for job security. If they truly worked together, if they truly stood as one, they couls bring in a new age. So what if a single dragonblooded can not take down a solar dawn or match a twilight in artifact making. If one is not enough, there are ten thousand dragons to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presenting the Empress as a blight who was doing nothing but holding them back is pretty unfair to both the Empress and to the Realm (which is, after all, her creation.)<br /> <br /> But the issue here isn't one of power but <i>unity</i>. It's meaningless to ask what the DBs could do if united in a vacuum. Yes, if every DB was connected to a singular hivemind that subsumed all their desires into a single common will, they could accomplish amazing things - but that wouldn't be the Dragon-Blooded as we know them in any meaningful sense, it'd just be a hivemind wearing their skins. The fractious nature, the divisions and squabbling and disagreements, all of these things are not unfortunate problems the DBs are saddled with, but rather central to what it means to be an entire host or race of people rather than a tiny number of individuals.<br /> <br /> Now, could someone unify them more effectively than the Empress did...? Could someone build a better Dragon-Blooded state than the Realm? Possibly! It is certainly something to shoot for in a Dragon-Blooded game. But you have to realize the enormity of what you're aiming for - your overall tone comes off as way too dismissive of the Empress and the Realm. In a typical Dragon-Blooded game, &quot;united the Dragon Blooded as well as the Emperss did&quot; would be a vast goal that could consume the entire story simply to achieve in a halting, imperfect way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if what is here is true, then the terrestrials are fractuous. Needing a celestial to lead them to do anything great. And that is rather..... deprotagonizing </div> </div> </div>First, nobody is saying they need a Celestial. The Celestials all face similar problems in slightly different ways (since it cuts at one of the core underlying themes of Exalted as a game.) A Celestial's toolbox for holding onto and wielding political power is slightly different (more raw-power charms, less access to dynastic stuff), but the core issue remains the same, and by default I'd expect them to repeat many of the Empress' mistakes.<br /> <br /> Second, again, you're dismissing the <i>entire Realm</i> here (when you say &quot;oh, so DBs can't do anything great?&quot; The Realm is great! I mean, for a certain definition of great (the &quot;Alexander the Great&quot; definition, obviously), but it's a big deal. Yes, it's not completely unthinkable to aim for doing even better, even in a purely Dragon-Blooded game, but... that's not really a question of Dragon-Blooded and power levels, that's a question of societies and philosophy and rulership. From a certain perspective the Realm is an amazing achievement. From another perspective, I'd argue that even mortals, left to their own devices, could make something better - the Realm's problems aren't really things that can be resolved by throwing more Essence at them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T02:15:35-07:00","id":1151247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1150951#post1150951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No number of helpful Exalted will make the world any smaller. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> .....<br /> <br /> \u200bBarring occasions where part of the plan literally entails making the world small enough for a single polity to effectively govern.</div> </div> </div> </div>This reminds me of a thread in the Exalted IRC channel where we were discussing ways to drastically lower shipping costs (eg. shooting packages out of giant cannons, etc.)<br /> <br /> My ultimate solution was to catastrophically lower the earth's population so the survivors can live very close to each other, thereby significantly lowering shipping costs.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T03:57:54-07:00","id":1151261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1151247#post1151247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My ultimate solution was to catastrophically lower the earth's population so the survivors can live very close to each other, thereby significantly lowering shipping costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmmm....<br /> <br /> I don't want to hijack this thread.<br /> <br /> \u200bSo, united Dragon Blooded:<br /> <br /> \u200bDo people envision the Dragon Blooded as a whole working on a small number of very big things, or as being able to work on many, many less big things spread across a wider area?<br /> <br /> \u200bThe latter is really what I've seen it as for quite a while; that the numbers of Dragon Blooded afford you scope and volume, while still not exactly raising the threshold of their capabilities.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat can be part of why a task such as taking over the world would be difficult even if they were all unreservedly working together but their numbers weren't much greater.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T09:07:08-07:00","id":1151345,"title":"","content":"I think a good question might be: <br /> <br /> What kind of devastating calamity would catalyze the Dragon Blooded host into a unified force? <br /> <br /> New Yozi from beyond the edge of the world? Another Balorian Crusade? The Abyssals leading the entire population of the underworld in a campaign to destroy creation? The Loom of Fate collapsing under the strain of fighting Sidereals and Getimians tearing fate apart? <br /> <br /> Nothing will <i>ever</i> completely force any bureaucratic monstrosity such as the realm to <i>completely </i>abandon politics even in the face of utter destruction, but there's nothing that unites disparate factions like a common enemy. So long as you've got a good leader and enough forewarning and evidence of the problem that you can actually convince people of its threat level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-20T09:51:17-07:00","id":1151369,"title":"","content":"It's worth noting, unless the new Edition decides to change it, that the exact level of contentiousness and division in the Scarlet Dynasty is something that was cultivated by the policies of the Empress; there's a certain artificial scarcity to force competition over resources going on there.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe assumptions that the policy was based off of, that it was necessary to ensure the long-term survival of the Realm and/or herself, lest some other contended become secure enough to make an attempt on her life, is not unreasonable, if obviously somewhat biased. She wouldn't be the first autocrat who responded to an assassination attempt by going a bit overboard and applying some attribution errors. After all, the initial written history of the Realm had it that a lot of, if not most, Dragon Blooded responded to the Great Contagion by actually working together to rebuild the Realm, and given some of the characterisations given, I attribute that to more sophisticated reasons than everybody being afraid that they were going to be blown up next.<br /> <br /> \u200bIt would be difficult to do that with the current Realm, because it is primarily inhabited by people who have been brought up conditioned to accept that environment of division and violence, but there are conceivably ways of getting it to work that don't even require wiping the slate clean. The Realm already does have a unifying mythos, and narratives to impel and structure ideas of duty and morality, you would just need people who would put in the hard work to more strongly emphasize and compel those into people's attitudes, show a willingness to trust them, and not respond to the occasional disaster with &quot;1% chance treated as absolute certainty&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for the idea of extending authority over the world, I would say that depends a bit on the ideological basis of that goal, or at least the framework provided to get people to do it. For instance, pushing an agenda of entitled militarism can be the sort of thing that can have a lot of the necessary actors seek their own interests to the detriment of their peers.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T14:00:01-07:00","id":1152606,"title":"","content":"Something else to consider is that, at least by the developers thread, all Exalted who took part in the War was affected by the Great Curse. That would include the Terrestrials. Do we know what those effects are, and what bearing it would have on this discussion?<br /> <br /> It strikes me as... interesting that at least one known manifestation of the Curse in 2nd Edition--the Sidereal Curse--specifically curtailed the ability of the Exalts to coordinate. The Solar Curse was the same, if you believe the Curse tended to megalomania or other antisocial (to say the least) behavior that would impede unity.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the 'big squabbling family' aspect (NPI) of the Terrestrials is the Curse's manifestation for them. It certainly impedes unity and coordination--the very attributes which allowed the Exalts to win the War--and this would hold true for the Shogunate as well as the Empress's Realm. That last assumes that the Shogun/Daimyo nomenclature is deliberately used in Exalted as a call to Sengoku Jidai Japan, which would definitely qualify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3551-ulthwithian","name":"Ulthwithian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T14:09:19-07:00","id":1152608,"title":"","content":"The terrestrials got something like a watered down version of the Solars. Apparently it's not a limit break type thing but they get splat-xp if they act in a way commensurate with the curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T14:36:58-07:00","id":1152614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1152608#post1152608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The terrestrials got something like a watered down version of the Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, that's just the Water Aspects. <br /> <br /> (sorry)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T14:50:51-07:00","id":1152617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1150564-what-can-the-dragonblooded-host-do-when-united?p=1152614#post1152614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nah, that's just the Water Aspects.<br /> <br /> (sorry)</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I feel like this Dragonblooded Great Curse discussion got off to a rocky start. Before things get heated I'd like to think we can all find a greener pasture in discussion once the book is released and we've all had a chance to catch our breathe. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> ....sorry not sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2997,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/","user":"Guest","date":". 10-24-2017, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}